WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.460
Open U and the conventional rack unit are different vertical grids.

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.700
The O R V three base specification describes forty-eight millimeter Open U

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.380
spacing and forty-four point four-five millimeter rack-unit spacing.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.820
The difference accumulates across a stack, so these labels aren't interchangeable ways

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:16.480
to count height.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.100
The selected rack features, supports and equipment mounting arrangement determine what can

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:21.720
be installed.

8
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.140
An adapter can address a defined mechanical interface, but it doesn't automatically

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.060
establish the power connector location, service access or cooling arrangement.

10
00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.560
Review those separately.

11
00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.500
For a mixed-equipment proposal, mark the grid used by each item and

12
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.440
the reference used to locate its connections.

13
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.300
Check both the occupied envelope and the required installation movement.

14
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.240
Avoid inferring compatibility from the number printed next to U on a

15
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:45.840
product sheet.

16
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.740
The practical outcome is a stack arrangement that is supported and aligned

17
00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:53.360
at every required interface, rather than a height total that happens to

18
00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.280
fit inside the frame.

